{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.colourCurve_branch_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.colourCurve_branch_defect","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L96-L102","doc":"**The branch defect is `qou-fi93`'s `(10/27)·z·(4z² + 3)`** — so that\nquantity is a difference between the two square roots of one `q`, not between\n`q` and `1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.colourCurve_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.colourCurve_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L91-L94","doc":"**`r` is exactly bar-invariant.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.colourCurve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.colourCurve","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L87-L89","doc":"The colour curve `r(z) = (5/27)(4z³ + 3z² + 3z + 4)` (`qou-ndt5`; the same\n`q_W(z)` as `t-duality-elliptic.md`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.bar_invariant_of_zOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.bar_invariant_of_zOf","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L81-L85","doc":"Any function of `z` is therefore bar-invariant — stated for an arbitrary\n`f`, so it covers `r` and every other quantity built from the modulus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.zOf_branchSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.zOf_branchSwap","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L75-L79","doc":"**The branch NEGATES `z`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.zOf_barLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.zOf_barLift","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**The bar FIXES `z`.**  This is the load-bearing fact.\n\nNo `s ≠ 0` hypothesis is needed: in a field `0⁻¹ = 0`, so both sides are `0`\nat `s = 0` and the identity is unconditional.  Stated that way deliberately —\ncarrying a hypothesis the proof does not use would invite a reader to think\nthe bar-invariance is conditional on something. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.branchSwap_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.branchSwap_sq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L59-L62","doc":"`branchSwap` fixes `q = s²` — it is the other root of the SAME `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.barLift_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.barLift_sq","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L54-L57","doc":"`barLift` really does invert `q = s²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.branchSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.branchSwap","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L51-L52","doc":"The branch swap: the *other* square root of the same `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.barLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.barLift","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L47-L49","doc":"The substrate bar `q ↦ 1/q`, lifted to `s`.  `qou-ndt5`: this is the\nunique lift preserving the degeneration locus `s² + s − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.zOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveBarVsBranch.zOf","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveBarVsBranch.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The colour-curve modulus `z = s − 1/s`, with `s² = q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}